fied)\n\nNone of these truths is behavior-dependent in the sense of Step 3. `deadline_after` is a pure arithmetic function with no state transition, cancellation or ordering invariant, so presence plus passing tests is sufficient evidence.\n\n### Task 1 decision gate (retry budget choice)\n\nTreated as resolved, per the run context: no human operator was available (unattended DevFlow run), and DevFlow resumed the orchestrator to make the choice. The orchestrator chose 120 s. SUMMARY.md records this accurately (key-decisions: \"resolved by the orchestrator, not a human operator\"). It is not a human_needed item.\n\nI also checked the choice against the plan's own stated constraints: 30 s is below the 90 s failover window, 300 s is above the 240 s pager threshold, and 120 s is the only offered value that satisfies both. The code comment in `probe/budget.py` matches the plan and SUMMARY.\n\n### Negative controls\n\n- Scratch copy of `HEAD` (via `git archive`) with the constant changed from 120 to 77: the suite fails (`AssertionError: 77 not found in (30, 120, 300)`, `FAILED (failures=1)`, exit 1). So the tests do catch an out-of-range constant. Scratch directory removed.\n- My first test invocation used `python3 -I`, which removes the current directory from `sys.path`, giving `ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'probe'`. That came from my flag, not from the repo. The plan's actual command (without `-I`) passes.\n\n### Required Artifacts\n\n| Artifact | Expected | Status | Details |\n| -------- | -------- | ------ | ------- |\n| `probe/budget.py` | `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` and `deadline_after` | VERIFIED | `verify.artifacts`: 1/1 passed. 11 lines, substantive, imported by both test modules. |\n| `probe/__init__.py` | Empty package marker | VERIFIED | Exists, 0 bytes (commit `488de6a`: `probe/__init__.py | 0`). |\n\n### Key Link Verification\n\nThe plan declares no `must_haves.key_links` (`verify.key-links` exit 66, not applicable). Manual check: both test modules import `probe.budget` and the import resolves at runtime. There is no production caller in this phase's scope, and none is required by the goal.\n\n### Data-Flow Trace (Level 4)\n\nNot applicable. The phase renders no dynamic data. It defines a constant and a pure function.\n\n### Behavioral Spot-Checks\n\n| Behavior | Command | Result | Status |\n| -------- | ------- | ------ | ------ |\n| Constant value and type | `python3 -c \"import probe.budget as b; ...\"` | `120 <class 'int'>` | PASS |\n| Helper arithmetic | same, `deadline_after(10.0)` | `130.0` | PASS |\n| Full suite | `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -v` | 6 tests, OK, exit 0 | PASS |\n| Suite catches a bad constant (negative control) | same command on a copy with 77 | exit 1 | PASS (fails as it must) |\n\n### Probe Execution\n\nSKIPPED: the phase declares no probe scripts. `probe/` is the Python package under test, not a `probe-*.sh` check.\n\n### Requirements Coverage\n\n| Requirement | Source Plan | Description | Status | Evidence |\n| ----------- | ----------- | ----------- | ------ | -------- |\n| BUDGET-01 | 01-01-PLAN.md (`requirements: [BUDGET-01]`) | `probe.budget` defines `DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` from 30/120/300, and `deadline_after` returns `start_secs + DEFAULT_RETRY_BUDGET_SECS` | SATISFIED | Truths 2 and 3. REQUIREMENTS.md lists BUDGET-01 as the only v1 requirement and maps it to Phase 1. No orphaned requirements. |\n\n### Anti-Patterns Found\n\nNone in `probe/` or `tests/`. Searched for `TBD|FIXME|XXX|TODO|HACK`: no matches, so the debt-marker gate is clear. No stubs, empty returns or placeholder code.\n\n### Human Verification Required\n\nNone.\n\n### Gaps Summary\n\nNo gaps. The phase goal is achieved: the module defines a default budget of 120 s (one of the three offered values) and a `deadline_after` helper that adds it to a start time.\n\n## What this verification does not establish\n\n- That 120 s is the right business value. The 90 s failover and 4-minute pager figures come from the plan text; neither SUMMARY.md nor I could independently check them. The tests only check \"one of 30/120/300\" and the addition. If those figures are wrong, the choice should be revisited. This is not a defect found in the code.\n- That `deadline_after` is correct against a real clock or real callers. No caller exists in this phase.\n- The 4 extra tests in `tests/test_budget_deadline.py` were added after execution by the Nyquist validation step, not by the plan. They strengthen the evidence for truth 3 but are outside the plan's `files_modified`.\n\n## Advisory (not blocking)\n\nCode review (`01-REVIEW.md`) reported 3 warnings and 3 info items. All six are still `open` in `01-REVIEW-DISPOSITION.md`, so none has been triaged. None contradicts a must-have. I did not re-review them, but I confirmed WR-01's premise is consistent with the roadmap: the ROADMAP criterion uses `-s tests`, which works. A bare `python3 -m unittest discover` (no `-s`) is the case the review says finds no tests.\n\n- WR-01: bare `python3 -m unittest discover` finds zero tests (no `tests/__init__.py`).\n- WR-02: `deadline_after` accepts any value; time base undocumented.\n- WR-03: `.planning/milestone.lock` and `.planning/state.json` are untracked and un-ignored (confirmed by `git status`).\n\n---\n\n_Verified: 2026-10-20T19:30:00Z_\n_Verifier: Claude (gsd-verifier)_\n\n.gitignore\ndevflow.toml\nprobe/__init__.py\nprobe/budget.py\ntests/test_budget.py\ntests/test_budget_deadline.py","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017VzMA287qdojso29GTfYuT","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
